---
import Legal from '../../components/Legal.astro';
---
<Legal
  site="agency"
  title="Privacy Policy — Tisvia Marketing"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Tisvia Marketing collects, uses and protects the information you share with us."
  updated="10 November 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what information Tisvia Marketing collects, why, and what we do with it.
    It covers this website and the enquiries and client work that follow from it.
  </p>

  <h2>What this website collects</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Nothing.</strong> This site has no contact form, no login, no advertising pixel and no
    analytics script. It sets no cookies. Nothing you do on the page is recorded by us.
  </p>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Vercel. Like any web host, Vercel's servers process the standard request
    information needed to deliver a page — your IP address, the page requested, your browser type
    and the time of the request. We do not use this for tracking or profiling.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect when you contact us</h2>
  <p>
    When you message us on WhatsApp, email us or reach us on Instagram or LinkedIn, we receive
    whatever you choose to send: typically your name, your phone number or email address, your
    business details and what you want help with.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect as your agency</h2>
  <p>If you become a client, we may also handle:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Billing details and payment records.</li>
    <li>Access to your advertising, analytics and business accounts, where you grant it.</li>
    <li>Campaign data, leads and customer enquiries generated by the campaigns we run for you.</li>
    <li>Brand assets, product information and anything else you share for the work.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To answer your enquiry and quote for the work.</li>
    <li>To plan, run, optimise and report on your campaigns.</li>
    <li>To invoice you and keep the accounting records the law requires.</li>
    <li>To contact you about work in progress.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell your information, and we do not share it with anyone for their own marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
  <p>
    Running campaigns means using other companies' platforms. Depending on the work, your data may
    pass through Meta (Facebook and Instagram), Google (Google Ads and Analytics), WhatsApp, email
    providers and payment processors. Each handles data under its own privacy policy, and we use
    only what the work requires.
  </p>
  <p>
    Lead data produced by your campaigns belongs to you. We access it only to run and report on the
    campaigns.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Enquiries that do not become work are kept for up to two years. Client records are kept for the
    length of the engagement and afterwards for as long as tax and accounting law requires. Access
    to your advertising and business accounts is handed back or removed when the engagement ends —
    ask us and we will remove it sooner.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable care with the information you give us and limit access to the people doing
    the work. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee
    absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us what we hold about you, ask for it to be corrected, or ask us to delete it, as
    far as the law allows us to. Write to the email address below and we will respond within 30
    days. You can stop messaging us at any time, and ask to be removed from any list.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our services are for businesses. We do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 18.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. The date at the top of the page shows when it last changed.
  </p>
</Legal>
